.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtokenbooth\fR opens a site's login page in a locked\-down browser window and hands the
token the login leaves behind to the shell that asked for it.
.PP
Every request goes to the tokenbooth daemon, and is served only for a shell in which
\fBpidvault\fR(1) has unlocked the vault the profile names. The daemon answers \fBget\fR from
its cache while the token is valid. Otherwise it opens a booth: Google Chrome as a fresh
dynamic user that owns nothing, drawing through the caller's Wayland connection, allowed to
navigate only to the profile's hosts, and gone once the token appears.
.PP
Cookies named in \fIkeep_cookies\fR are kept from one login to the next, so that a provider
can remember the device. They and the token are sealed with a key kept in the profile's
vault, and only the daemon and the booth ever see them; the client sees only the token.
.PP
The window opens only on Wayland. On X11, where any client can read what is typed, it is
refused.
.SH PROFILES
A profile is a TOML file, stored with \fBtokenbooth profile set\fR \fINAME FILE\fR:
.TP
\fBstart_url\fR
The login page.
.TP
\fBcookie\fR
The name of the cookie that holds the token.
.TP
\fBcookie_domain\fR
The domain that cookie is set for. Default: the host of \fIstart_url\fR without \fBwww.\fR
.TP
\fBvia\fR
Identity providers the login passes through, whose hosts are allowed as well: \fBgoogle\fR,
\fBmicrosoft\fR.
.TP
\fBallowed_hosts\fR
Hosts the window may navigate to, as globs. Default: the host of \fIstart_url\fR and its
subdomains.
.TP
\fBkeep_cookies\fR
Cookies to keep for the next login, as \fINAME\fR@\fIDOMAIN\fR globs, for instance
\fB*@google.com\fR. The token cookie is never kept.
.TP
\fBdone_url\fR
A regular expression the page's URL must match before the token is taken.
.TP
\fBuser_agent\fR
A user agent to claim instead of Chrome's own.
.TP
\fBtimeout\fR
Seconds before the window gives up; 0 for never. Default: 600.
.TP
\fBvault\fR
The pidvault vault that must be unlocked to use or change the profile, and that holds its
key. Default: \fBdefault\fR.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
start_url     = "https://gopro.com/login"
cookie        = "gp_access_token"
via           = ["google"]
keep_cookies  = ["*@google.com", "*@*.google.com"]
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
The token was printed or written.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The window was closed without a token.
.TP
\fB2\fR
An error, or the request was refused.
.TP
\fB3\fR
The window timed out.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/run/pidvault/stored/VAULT/tokenbooth/PROFILE.key\fR
The profile's key, made on first use. Without it the sealed state cannot be opened, and the
next login starts afresh.
.TP
\fI/run/pidvault/stored/VAULT/tokens/PROFILE\fR
Where \fB\-\-to\-vault\fR writes the token.
.TP
\fI/var/lib/tokenbooth/UID/\fR
The daemon's state for each user: profiles, and each profile's sealed token and kept cookies.
.TP
\fI/run/tokenbooth/sock\fR
The daemon's socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpidvault\fR(1), \fBjournalctl\fR(1): \fBjournalctl \-u tokenbooth \-u 'tokenbooth\-booth@*'\fR
